[180.986338, "o", "    \u001b[2mUsage: mailman conf [OPTIONS]\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mTry 'mailman conf -h' for help.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mError: No such option: -l\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mUsage: mailman conf [OPTIONS]\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m  Print the Mailman configuration.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mOptions:\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m  -o, --output FILENAME  File to send the output to.  If not given, or if '-'\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m                         is given, standard output is used.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m  -s, --section TEXT     Section to use for the lookup.  If no key is given,\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m                         all the key-value pairs of the given section will be\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m                         displayed.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m  -k, --key TEXT         Key to use for the lookup.  If no section is given,\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m                         all the key-values pair from any section matching the\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m                         given key will be displayed.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m  -h, --help             Show this message and exit.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
