[482.678601, "o", "\u001b[37m+token\u001b[0m"]
[482.691551, "o", "\u001b[37m@...\u001b[0m"]
[482.723657, "o", "\u001b[37m  (conf\u001b[0m"]
[482.74436, "o", "\u001b[37mirmation replies\u001b[0m"]
[482.762957, "o", "\u001b[37m)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[483.607385, "o", "\u001b[37m```\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[37m## Files changed\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[37m**`/etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg`**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m- `site_owner: postmaster@local.edu`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m- `[mta] configuration: /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg` (self-reference so the `[postfix]` section lives in the required config file)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37m- appended `[postfix]` section with `transport_file_type: regex` so Mailman generates Postfix **regexp** transport entries, which correctly route `reading-group-confirm+<token>@local.edu` (and `-bounces+...`) to LMTP.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[37m**Postfix (`main.cf`/`master.cf`)**\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[483.607463, "o", "\u001b[37m```\u001b[0m"]
[483.629176, "o", "\r\n\u001b[37mmyhostname = local.edu\u001b[0m"]
[483.64326, "o", "\r\n\u001b[37mmydomain = local\u001b[0m"]
[483.674921, "o", "\u001b[37m.edu\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37mmydestination\u001b[0m"]
[483.68349, "o", "\u001b[37m = local.edu\u001b[0m"]
[483.702414, "o", "\u001b[37m, localhost, local\u001b[0m"]
[483.727897, "o", "\u001b[37mhost.localdomain\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[37mtransport\u001b[0m"]
[483.839263, "o", "\u001b[35m_\u001b[0m\u001b[35mmaps = regexp:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35mlocal\u001b[0m"]
[483.852861, "o", "\u001b[35m_\u001b[0m\u001b[35mrecipient_maps =\u001b[0m"]
[483.892126, "o", "\u001b[37m proxy:unix:\u001b[0m"]
[483.894483, "o", "\u001b[37mpasswd.byname $\u001b[0m"]
[483.944184, "o", "\u001b[37malias\u001b[0m"]
[483.970024, "o", "\u001b[35m_\u001b[0m\u001b[35mmaps regexp:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp\u001b[0m"]
[483.991109, "o", "\r\n\u001b[37mmaillog\u001b[0m"]
[486.28383, "o", "\u001b[35m_\u001b[0m\u001b[35mfile = /var/log/postfix.log\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- chroot disabled for all master.cf services (container-friendly access to Mailman's generated maps).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- `postfix` user added to the `list` group and `/var/lib/mailman3/data` made traversable so the map is readable.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m**Mailman list state**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- Created `reading-group@local.edu` (owner `root@local.edu`).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- `subscription_policy = open` (no owner approval; unverified addresses still get a confirmation mail)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- `unsubscription_policy = confirm` (leave requires replying to the confirmation mail)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- `archive_policy = never`, member/non-member post actions `accept`\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m**Services**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- Mailman master running as `list` (PID 1079, LMTP on `127.0.0.1:8024`, REST on `:8001`)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- Postfix master running (PID 904, SMTP on `:25`)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m## Verification performed\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m- Direct mail to a fresh unix user lands in `/var/mail/<user>` (mbox).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- Join: sending to `reading-group-join@` leaves user *unsubscribed*; confirmation mail from `reading-group-confirm+<token>@local.edu` with subject `...join...`; replying subscribes them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- Post: mail to `reading-group@` is delivered to every subscriber's mailbox with `[Reading-group]` subject prefix.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- Leave: sending to `reading-group-leave@` leaves user subscribed until they reply to the `...leave...` confirmation; after replying they are removed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[35m- List is currently clean (0 members) and both daemons are running.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[35m`python3 /app/eval.py` passes all its tests.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
